WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.720
Wondering what to watch tonight?

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:05.270
There are a bunch of underrated films you
may have missed so far this year and they're

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.740
really worth checking out.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.520
Here are a few hidden gems that may have flown
under your radar in 2019.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.400
The whip-smart comedy Egg stars Alysia Reiner
as an artist named Tina, and Gbenga Akinnagbe

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.180
as her husband, Wayne.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.859
Mad Men's Christina Hendricks plays Karen,
Tina's so-called "best friend" from art school

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.540
a compulsively cruel mother-to-be who says
things like this:

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.300
"It can be weird when you're with people who
don't have children."

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.630
Tina thinks she's gained the upper hand when
she invites Karen and her husband Doug played

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.340
by David Alan Basche over to her New York
loft to make a major announcement:

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.900
"We're having a baby too, yay."

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.340
"Oh my...God!"

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:45.300
That's thanks to the bubbly blonde surrogate
Kiki, portrayed by Anna Camp.

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.510
She may seem ditzy, but she's certainly not
innocent.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.510
"Here, let me..."

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:49.510
"Oh my god, yeah!"

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:50.960
"I can see why you guys chose her."

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:51.460
"Oh, shut up."

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.360
"I'll… get you something to put on."

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.140
"Hiiii…

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:55.640
I'm Kiki."

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.640
Full of biting wit and sharp social commentary,
Egg is a fiercely funny comedy of manners

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.140
that brilliantly explores the weirdness of
motherhood.

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:08.600
Directed by Steven Soderbergh, High Flying
Bird slyly subverts the sports movie genre

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.320
in a way that's both stylish and admirably
risky.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.020
The film centers around sports agent Ray Burke,
portrayed by André Holland.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.680
After he discovers a loophole during a professional
basketball league lockout, Ray hatches a plan

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:23.521
that could help him advance his career and
fulfill his obligations to Erick, his young

00:01:23.521 --> 00:01:24.590
basketball client.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:28.680
The prospect of forever changing the world
of pro basketball proves hard to resist...

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.300
"Man, I could see a whole infrastructure that
put the control back in the hands of those

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.160
behind the ball, instead of those up in the
sky box."

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.740
Shot entirely on an iPhone, High Flying Bird
has the kind of sleek aesthetic and structure

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:44.700
that grabs you by the wrist and pushes you
straight down the rabbit hole.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.020
The film hit Netflix in early February, right
after Velvet Buzzsaw and Russian Doll premiered.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:53.030
A lot of viewers probably missed out on High
Flying Bird because they simply had too many

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.500
options to choose from.

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:57.260
The good news is: you can watch it on Netflix
right now.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.000
Score!

00:01:58.580 --> 00:02:03.340
In A Vigilante, actress Olivia Wilde plays
Sadie, a domestic abuse survivor who sets

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.900
out to save other victims from their violent
partners.

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.240
Meanwhile, she continues to hunt down her
vile husband, portrayed by Morgan Spector.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.420
He's such a despicable man, no one dares speak
his name out loud.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.360
"My husband, he would set my bones after…"

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:17.890
"After he broke them."

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.780
"And I broke the rules."

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.200
A Vigilante is explosive, gritty, and a fantastic
showcase of Wilde's talents.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:28.010
Reviews have been hugely positive, with RogerEbert.com
claiming that:

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:31.500
"Wilde's performance is so committed that
there are times when you may fear for her

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.570
physical safety and emotional health."

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:39.050
Mel Gibson and Vince Vaughn portray two embattled
police detectives in Dragged Across Concrete

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.840
a film that's certainly bleak, but also quite
good.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.080
"A single red ant could have eaten it faster."

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.599
That's about all the humor you get in this
one.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:50.760
The gritty drama unfolds after the two men
get unnecessarily rough with a suspect and

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.420
his girlfriend during a drug bust.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.440
When video footage of the incident gets leaked
to the press, both detectives are suspended

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.640
from the force without pay.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:02.200
With no means of legally making money, they
begin mapping out a dangerous plan and things

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.100
get very real very fast.

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:08.880
While some viewers might find Dragged Across
Concrete too brutal and mean-spirited, audiences

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:12.920
who caught the film during its limited release
were genuinely impressed and so were many

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:13.480
critics.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.200
Entertainment Weekly hailed the film, assuring
readers that

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.560
"[If you're] wondering where this is all headed,
you won’t be disappointed when it finally

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.280
gets there."

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.340
To Dust strikes just the right balance of
strangeness.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:28.160
The directorial debut of Shawn Snyder, it's
an oddball dramedy that's truly refreshing

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:28.740
and original.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.660
The story revolves around Hasidic cantor Shmuel,
portrayed by Géza Röhrig.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.680
Since losing his wife, Shmuel has been experiencing
unsettling nightmares about her dead body.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:41.590
Desperate to find some peace of mind, he recruits
a community college biology instructor named

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:46.060
Albert portrayed by Matthew Broderick hoping
he'll teach him what happens to the body after

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:46.560
death.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.100
"I fear her soul is suffering…

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.740
She returns to the earth."

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:55.940
This unlikely pair engage in some bizarre
experiments and morbid misadventures in an

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.200
effort to soothe Shmuel's boundless anxiety.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.300
To Dust is a film everyone should see.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:04.280
It's marvelously strange, truly original,
and unmistakably human.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.480
Written and directed by Christian Petzold,
Transit utterly captivated audiences during

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.420
its limited release in March 2019.

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:16.400
This moving drama tells the story of Georg,
a refugee fleeing Germany and heading to France

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.560
as fascism rises in his home country.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.860
Georg is supposed to meet a writer named Weidel
in Paris, but he soon discovers that the man

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.860
has committed suicide.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.140
Georg then assumes the writer's identity and
scoops up his belongings, boarding a train

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.380
to Marseille, a port city teeming with other
refugees.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:35.860
Once there, Georg ends up meeting Marie, a
woman desperately searching for her lost husband

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.820
— who just so happens to be Weidel.

00:04:38.229 --> 00:04:42.820
Transit is a genuinely moving film that garnered
loads of praise from critics, with Film Inquiry

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:43.420
calling it

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.540
"A film of surreal, sad beauty [that] should
not be missed."

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.009
If there was any justice in the world, The
Kid Who Would Be King would have reigned supreme

00:04:51.009 --> 00:04:52.009
at the box office.

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:54.920
But alas, the film went largely unnoticed
upon its release.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.740
Written and directed by Joe Cornish, The Kid
Who Would Be King puts a modern spin on a

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.860
very familiar tale.

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:04.940
Louis Ashbourne Serkis plays 12-year-old student
Alex Elliot, who discovers he's the only person

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:07.969
on the planet who can pull the mighty sword
Excalibur out from its stone.

00:05:07.969 --> 00:05:12.210
It's the only weapon that can vanquish the
powerful sorceress Morgana, portrayed by Rebecca

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:12.700
Ferguson.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:16.640
Alex gathers up his friends to serve as his
knights, and the whole crew enlists the help

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:21.520
of a backwards-aging wizard named Merlin played
here by both Angus Imrie and Patrick Stewart.

00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:25.800
Together, they conspire to take down Morgana
before an impending solar eclipse lets her

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.240
enslave the people of England.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.940
"The sword chose you…"

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.260
"... Why would we help you?"

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:32.240
"Because you're the strongest people I know.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:32.740
You're my knights."

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.400
For whatever reason, The Kid Who Would Be
King was a critical success, but a commercial

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:37.900
failure.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.260
Although the movie lost millions of dollars
at the box office, you shouldn't let that

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:42.020
discourage you.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:45.900
Critics praised the film's inventiveness and
good-naturedness, with The Guardian writing

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:46.400
that

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.200
"This movie is sentimental in all the right
places, and impossible to dislike."

00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.720
This coming-of-age story is like nothing you've
seen before.

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:58.120
In Don't Come Back from the Moon, we meet
16-year-old Mickey, played by Jeffrey Wahlberg.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.979
The young man is grappling with a profound
sense of abandonment.

00:06:00.979 --> 00:06:05.120
His father played by James Franco is only
the latest man in their California town to

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:07.760
pack up his bags and leave, vanishing without
a trace.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:12.460
"It was as if he vaporized out of the driver's
seat and just… floated away."

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:16.720
It sounds like the plot of a sci-fi series,
but Don't Come Back from the Moon is rooted

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:20.909
in a harsh reality: the fathers and husbands
in this rundown desert community walk away

00:06:20.909 --> 00:06:22.899
from their lives because they have nothing
better to do.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.020
And they evidently don't care that they're
leaving their families behind.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.320
Everyone in this family reacts to the departure
in a different way.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:33.800
Mickey's mother portrayed by Rashida Jones
tries to resist self-medicating with alcohol.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.920
Meanwhile, Mickey does his best to look after
his younger brother, played by Zackary Arthur.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:42.800
Throughout the film, Mickey develops a considerable
rebellious steak, explores his sexuality,

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:44.840
and tries coming to grips with his strange
new life.

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:48.680
Released in a limited run in mid-January,
Don't Come Back from the Moon was praised

00:06:48.689 --> 00:06:50.610
by critics, with Variety writing that

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:55.460
"[The film is] an artful and affecting mix
of harshly defined specifics and impressionistic

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:56.260
storytelling."

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:01.879
An unlikely charmer about an unlikely friendship,
Paddleton debuted at the 2019 Sundance Film

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:05.940
Festival on February 1st before making its
way to Netflix later that month.

00:07:06.129 --> 00:07:09.939
The film stars Mark Duplass and Ray Romano
in roles that are unlike anything they've

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:10.700
done before.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.840
When Duplass's Michael Thompson is diagnosed
with terminal stomach cancer, it seriously

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:18.440
intensifies his friendship with neighbor Andy
Freeman, played by Romano.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:23.279
Best known as comedic actors, Duplass and
Romano prove to be equally adept at dramatic

00:07:23.279 --> 00:07:27.120
roles, giving themselves over to their characters
in a way that feels completely organic.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.099
What's most impressive about Paddleton is
its relative lack of dialogue, which immediately

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:34.060
distinguishes it from other dramas that involve
"The Big C."

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:43.900
"Okay."

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.900
As you can see, Michael and Andy both have
a serious aversion to small talk, which guarantees

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.080
that every spoken word is a meaningful one.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:55.999
Genuinely funny and heartbreaking, Paddleton
is a moving film from beginning to end.

00:07:55.999 --> 00:07:57.060
And guess what?

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.840
It's available on Netflix, so you can check
it out right now.

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:01.539
Just make sure you have a box of tissues handy.

00:08:02.559 --> 00:08:05.779
You probably haven't heard of The Standoff
at Sparrow Creek until now.

00:08:05.779 --> 00:08:09.770
The film didn't generate a whole lot of buzz
upon its release, even though it certainly

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.759
earned a whole lot of favorable reviews.

00:08:11.759 --> 00:08:16.809
Henry Dunham's feature directorial debut centers
around an ex-cop named Gannon, who subsequently

00:08:16.809 --> 00:08:18.360
joined a militia in Michigan.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:22.659
The gruff gentleman, portrayed by James Badge
Dale, soon learns that somebody has just shot

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:23.680
up a police funeral.

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:26.800
What's worse, the shooter evidently belongs
to Gannon's militia.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.699
But which of these dangerous men did it?

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:32.900
Using his skills as an interrogator, Gannon
grills each member until one of them reveals

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.300
himself to be the cop killer.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.960
The film opened in a limited capacity in January,
a month that finds lots of films getting completely

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:39.460
buried.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.080
That's a real shame, too, because The Standoff
at Sparrow Creek deserves to be widely seen.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:45.640
Reviews were glowing, with The A.V.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:46.420
Club writing that

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:50.850
"[There's a] lean, punchy, beautifully shot
’70s-style thriller underneath the controversial

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:51.440
premise."

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:56.760
In the Icelandic survival film Arctic, Danish
actor Mads Mikkelsen plays a man who's lost,

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.700
alone, and running out of resources in the
Arctic Circle.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:04.140
He misses out on a chance to get rescued when
a helicopter meant to retrieve him crashes,

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.210
killing the pilot and injuring a passenger.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.960
Now he must choose between staying cooped
up in a crashed plane to survive, or traveling

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.280
through an arctic wasteland in the hopes of
saving himself and the passenger.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.060
Guess what he ultimately decides to do.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.200
"It's ok…"

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:28.700
Mikkelsen has described Arctic as one of the
most challenging projects he's ever been involved

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:32.810
with, and critics have assured that the grueling
days on location in Iceland were well worth

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:33.300
the effort.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:35.540
In its rapturous review, Seven Days wrote
that

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.460
"Mikkelsen gives an astonishingly expressive
performance in what is essentially a silent

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:39.960
film.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.400
[...] It'll be a cold day in hell before a
better chronicle of cold days in hell comes

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:43.900
along."

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:48.800
Starring Emile Hirsch and John Cusack, Never
Grow Old centers around Hirsch's undertaker

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:53.620
Patrick Tate and Cusack's ruthless outlaw
Dutch Albert, who soon stakes his claim on

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:56.460
the formerly quiet town of Garlow in 1849.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.660
Danny Webb plays Preacher Pike, who banned
alcohol, harlots, and gambling throughout

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.620
the town creating a kind of peace begging
to be broken.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.780
"Murderers need to be punished, Sheriff, 'fore
they drag this town into hell."

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:13.540
Dutch soon takes an interest in filling bottles
with liquor and saloons with working girls.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.490
And it isn't long before the death toll rises
and Dutch's viciousness drives Patrick to

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:17.980
violence.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:22.320
If you're a fan of Westerns, you'll want to
see Never Grow Old before you grow old yourself.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.880
The comedic chops of Madeleine Sami and Jackie
van Beek are on full display in The Breaker

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.780
Uppererers, a romantic comedy executive produced
by Taika Waititi.

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.760
Jen and Mel are two friends who have turned
their cynical views on romance into a lucrative

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:38.750
business venture: If you have the cash, they
can help you destroy your relationship in

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.860
next to no time.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.560
"It's simple, really.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:47.530
What we do is we take unhappy couples such
as yourself and consciously, forcibly and

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:49.160
irreversibly uncouple you."

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:54.940
The film opened in New Zealand theaters in
May 2018 and made its way to Netflix in February.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:58.370
Though the buddy comedy didn't make a huge
splash, critics couldn't get enough of its

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.520
wacky sense of humor.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:00.870
Stuff magazine raved:

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:04.600
"The Breaker Upperers is the funniest and
most likable film I've seen this year.

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:05.580
Go see it."

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.120
We wholeheartedly agree.

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:11.110
This is the perfect choice for your next Netflix-and-chill
date… particularly if you're looking to

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:12.420
break someone's heart.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:20.400
"Sheree don't wanna be with you no more / Sharee
don't wanna be with you no more…"

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:23.140
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.360
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
films are coming soon.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:30.720
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

